# .gitignore for omarchy-voxtype
#
# This repo is a dictation tool. The files it works next to on a real machine are
# a live API key and a verbatim record of everything the user has ever said out
# loud. Installing or testing this project necessarily moves files between the
# repo, ~/.config/voxtype/ and ~/.local/state/voxtype/, and that is exactly the
# motion that drags those files into the working tree. Every group below names
# the leak it prevents. Do not relax a rule to "just commit this one".

# ── Credentials ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The `gemini` pipeline stage reads a Google Generative Language API key from
# ~/.config/voxtype/gemini.key (mode 0600). It is never part of this repo and
# there is no example of it — the README tells you to create it by hand.
gemini.key
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Dictation content: everything the user has ever said ────────────────────
# bin/voxtype-punct appends one JSON object per dictation — raw ASR text AND
# polished text — to ~/.local/state/voxtype/history.jsonl. History.qml reads it.
# A single copy into the repo would publish the user's entire spoken history.
history.jsonl
*.jsonl

# voxtype's meeting mode keeps its transcript index in
# ~/.local/share/voxtype/meetings/index.db. Same content class, SQLite instead.
meetings/
index.db
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# ── Live machine state, not shippable config ────────────────────────────────
# The real config.toml carries an absolute /home/<username> path to the wrapper
# and hardware-specific tuning; ship config/config.toml.example instead.
config.toml
config/config.toml
# The current pipeline spec, written by the bar panel. Personal, not a default.
polish-mode
# The user's own installed copies of the opt-in examples.
polish-sed.sed
config/polish-sed.sed
polish-prompt.local.txt
config/polish-prompt.local.txt

# ── Backup churn ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# voxtype and the panel both write timestamped backups next to the file they
# edit (config.toml.bak.pastekeys.1786717159, polish-mode.bak.1785264160, ...).
# Those backups contain the same secrets and state as the originals.
*.bak
*.bak.*
*.bak-*
*.orig
*.rej
*~

# ── Audio and models: never in git ──────────────────────────────────────────
# The batch-transcribe helper in bin/ converts its input to a 16 kHz mono WAV.
# Recorded audio is dictation content with the voice still attached to it.
*.wav
*.mp3
*.m4a
*.ogg
*.opus
*.flac
*.webm

# ASR and LLM weights live in ~/.local/share/voxtype/models and /var/lib/ollama.
# They are large, redistributable only under their own licences, and never ours.
models/
*.bin
*.onnx
*.gguf
*.safetensors
*.pt

# ── Scratch and internal notes ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# docs/ is where session notes go in the sibling plugin repos. Untracked there,
# untracked here — internal notes are not plugin documentation.
docs/
*.tmp
*.log
/tmp/

# ── Editor and OS noise ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
.idea/
.vscode/
